.TH KP-SYNC-CONFIG 5 "2026-10-28" "kp-sync 0.1.2" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
kp-sync-config \- TOML configuration for kp-sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default configuration is
.IR ~/.config/kp-sync/config.toml .
The
.B kp-sync --profile NAME
option selects
.IR ~/.config/kp-sync/NAME.toml .
An explicit
.B --config FILE
selects another TOML file. Profiles use the same schema; they do not migrate
or copy databases or history.
.PP
Unknown keys and values of the wrong type are rejected. Command settings are
argument arrays, never shell command strings. Keep secrets out of command
arguments and configuration files. Runtime state is private and stored under
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.SH TOP-LEVEL OPTIONS
.TP
.B hub
Database path used as the local synchronization hub. Defaults to
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pass.kdbx ;
named profiles default to
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/PROFILE/pass.kdbx .
.TP
.B hub_persistent
Boolean, default
.BR false .
Set true only when the configured hub is on an encrypted persistent disk.
.TP
.B require_encrypted
Boolean; defaults to the value of
.BR hub_persistent .
Require an encrypted filesystem for a persistent hub.
.TP
.B host
Machine name recorded in history. Defaults to the system hostname.
.TP
.B db_name
Database filename, default
.BR pass.kdbx .
Must be one filename, not a path.
.TP
.B key_file
KeePass key-file path, default
.IR ~/data/Personal/pass.keyx .
.SH ENDPOINTS
Use one
.B [[endpoints]]
table per copy. Common keys:
.TP
.B name
Unique endpoint name.
.TP
.B type
One of
.BR file ,
.BR rclone ,
or
.BR command .
.TP
.B enabled, readonly, optional
Booleans controlling endpoint use.
.TP
.B on_unavailable
Unavailable-endpoint policy.
.TP
.B timeout
Command/endpoint timeout in seconds.
.TP
.B foreign_writers
Whether other applications may change this copy. Defaults true for rclone
and read-write sessions.
.PP
For
.BR file ,
use
.B path
for a fixed database or
.B source = "runtime"
for the attached-drive endpoint. A runtime endpoint may also specify
.B identity
and only one enabled runtime file endpoint is allowed.
.PP
For
.BR rclone ,
use
.BR remote ,
.BR rclone_config ,
.BR download ,
.BR upload ,
.BR probe ,
and
.BR timeout
as required by the endpoint.
.B rclone_config
names a provider-owned file that is only read; kp-sync passes rclone its
own private per-profile copy and reports credentials unavailable while
no copy exists. For
.BR command ,
provide
.BR fetch ,
.BR store ,
and
.B probe
as argument arrays. The literal placeholders
.B {file}
and
.B {remote}
are substituted; no shell is used.
.SH NAMED SSH SESSIONS
Set
.B [sessions].enabled = true
to allow SSH sessions. Define one table per managed session:
.PP
.nf
[ssh_sessions.office]
target = "user@host:~/kp"
mode = "rw"
mount_dir = "~/kp"
unconfined = false
.fi
.TP
.B target
Required
.BR [USER@]HOST[:PATH]
destination. A path in the target overrides
.BR mount_dir .
.TP
.B mode
Either
.B ro
or
.BR rw ;
defaults to
.BR sessions.default_mode .
.TP
.B mount_dir
Remote mount path. Defaults to
.BR sessions.mount_dir .
.TP
.B unconfined
Boolean, default false. Disabling confinement requires an explicit true and
should be avoided.
.PP
Manage a named session with
.BR "kp-sync service start|stop|status ssh-session NAME" .
It uses a transient systemd user service, survives terminal closure, and
holds the SSH access and sync lease until stopped. It does not survive user
logout or reboot unless the systemd user manager is configured to linger.
Logs are in the systemd user journal.
.SS [sessions]
The shared settings are:
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean, default false.
.TP
.B mount_dir
Default remote mount path, default
.IR ~/kp .
.TP
.B tunnel_port
Reverse-tunnel port on the remote host, default 2222.
.TP
.B default_mode
Default access mode,
.B ro
or
.BR rw ;
default
.BR ro .
.TP
.B session_key_ttl
Session key lifetime in seconds, default 86400.
.SH KP-ACCESS OWNER SERVICES
Define a named owner process as an argv array:
.PP
.nf
[access_owners.windows]
command = ["/path/to/venv/bin/kp-access-owner", "--config", "/path/to/owner.toml"]
.fi
.PP
The command is started directly, without a shell, inside a transient systemd
user service and must remain in the foreground. Its stdout and stderr are
discarded; kp-sync lifecycle messages and errors are in the user journal.
Use an absolute executable path if the program is not in the systemd user
manager's
.BR PATH .
Manage it with
.BR "kp-sync service start|stop|status access-owner NAME" .
The owner must still be configured to use
.B kp-sync access-op
as its file-operation hook when synchronization integration is desired.
.SS [access]
.TP
.B staging_dir
Optional staging directory for kp-access.
.TP
.B db_path
Optional normalized absolute staged database path as seen by kp-access.
A directory component is preferred.
.SH USER INTERFACE
.SS [ui]
.TP
.B mode
One of
.BR auto ,
.BR tty ,
.BR gui ,
or
.BR none ;
default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B gui
GUI backend
.BR zenity ,
.BR kdialog ,
or a custom executable/argv array. Custom commands use a JSON
stdin/stdout protocol.
.TP
.B ask_first
Boolean, default true; ask before interrupting the user with a decision.
.TP
.B dialog_timeout
Decision dialog timeout in seconds, default 600.
.TP
.B notify
Boolean, default true.
.TP
.B progress
Boolean, default true. The delayed desktop progress window shows the profile
and configured hub path; hiding it does not cancel synchronization.
.SH OTHER SECTIONS
.SS [baseline]
.TP
.B stores
Endpoint names in priority order, default
.BR ["cloud", "pendrive"] .
Names resolve locally in each configuration; different machines may use
different aliases, but the same physical copy needs a consistent identity.
.TP
.B dir
History directory inside each baseline store, default
.BR kp-sync .
This one setting applies relative to every configured store's root.
Machines sharing a store must resolve to the same history directory.
Changing it does not migrate existing history.
.TP
.B keep_days
Retained history age in days, default 180.
.SS [drives]
.TP
.B notify_stale
Notify when an outdated attached drive is updated; default true.
.TP
.B directory
Relative database directory inside a mounted drive, default
.BR "." .
Absolute paths and parent traversal are rejected.
.TP
.B aliases
Optional per-profile display names in the nested
.B [drives.aliases]
table. Keys are complete
.B SERIAL:FS_UUID
identities and values must be non-empty strings without terminal control
characters. Aliases do not change synchronization identity, authorization,
mount matching or drive selection. Duplicate names are allowed; status
continues to show the technical identity.
.PP
.nf
[drives.aliases]
"1111222233334444:AB12-CD34" = "Daily backup"
.fi
.SS [credentials]
.TP
.B cache_timeout
Main password-keyring cache lifetime in seconds, default 900.
.SS [credentials.keepassxc]
.TP
.B url
Optional browser-protocol lookup URL. Configuring it opts into KeePassXC
retrieval before the manual cache and password prompt, when an operation
needs credentials. The URL is never fetched. Use one matching entry and
a unique hostname per profile, for example
.BR https://kp-sync-default.invalid .
Requires the optional
.B keepassxc
package extra, browser integration, and an unlocked KeePassXC database.
First interactive use requests association. Multiple matches warn and
fall back; locked or unavailable KeePassXC also falls back.
Silent polls skip lookup to avoid approval dialogs.
Retrieved passwords are validated but never cached across operations.
The configured key file remains required.
.PP
Only pairing metadata persists under
.BR $XDG_STATE_HOME/kp-sync/
(default
.IR ~/.local/state/kp-sync/ ),
privately isolated by configured host/profile and pinned to the selected
database identity. No password is stored there.
.B kp-sync keepassxc-disconnect
removes local pairing; revoke the connection in KeePassXC as well to
remove remote authorization.
.B kp-sync forget
only clears manually populated password caches.
.SS [backups]
.TP
.B keep
Number of runtime backups to retain, default 20.
.SS [verify]
.TP
.B max_entry_drop
Maximum fractional entry drop before confirmation may be required, default
.BR 0.10 .
.TP
.B min_entry_drop
Minimum entry drop threshold, default 5.
.TP
.B foreign_check
One of
.BR always
or
.BR merge-only ;
default
.BR always .
.SS [merge]
.TP
.B engine
One of
.BR kp-sync
or
.BR keepassxc ;
default
.BR kp-sync .
.TP
.B review
One of
.BR interactive ,
.BR auto-hub ,
.BR auto-other ,
or
.BR defer ;
default
.BR interactive .
.SS [daemon]
.TP
.B debounce
Hub-change debounce in seconds, default 2.
.TP
.B poll_interval
Endpoint polling interval in seconds, default 900; zero disables polling.
.TP
.B idle_exit
Exit delay after the last lease ends, default 120 seconds.
.TP
.B prestart_timeout
Application fast-start timeout, default 20 seconds.
.TP
.B access_lease_ttl
kp-access lease lifetime without requests, default 3600 seconds.
.TP
.B hub_path_unit
Install a systemd path unit for hub changes; default true.
.TP
.B idle_sync
Run periodic synchronization with no lease. Defaults true for persistent
hubs and false otherwise.
.TP
.B idle_sync_interval
Idle synchronization interval, default 3600 seconds.
.TP
.B rescue_wait
Time to wait for a removable drive during shutdown rescue, default 60
seconds.
.SS [sync]
.TP
.B lock_timeout
Engine lock timeout, default 60 seconds.
.TP
.B max_restarts
Maximum engine restarts after changing inputs, default 3.
.SS [launch]
.TP
.B default_app
Application launched by
.BR run ;
default
.BR keepassxc .
.TP
.B confirm_without_cloud
Boolean controlling launch confirmation if cloud access fails; default false.
.TP
.B quit_on_last_drive
Quit wrapper-launched applications after the last drive detaches; default
true.
.SS [apps.NAME]
Application-specific
.BR command ,
.BR process ,
.BR reloads ,
and
.B single_instance
settings. Commands are argument arrays. KeePassXC and keepass-legacy are
predefined.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kp-sync (1),
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
